                           Microsoft EntraID
                                 ----------> IAM in AWS

--> Microsoft Entra ID is Microsoft's cloud-based Identity and Access Management (IAM) service. It helps organizations manage users, groups, devices, applications, and access permissions securely.
--> Previously, Microsoft Entra ID was called Azure Active Directory (Azure AD). Microsoft renamed Azure AD to Entra ID in 2023

**Important Components of Microsoft Entra ID
1. Users
--> Represents employees, administrators, and guest users.
Example: admin@company.com
 
2. Groups
--> Organize users and assign permissions collectively.
Example: DevOps-Team, Azure-Admins.

3. MFA (Multi-Factor Authentication)
--> Requires additional verification during sign-in, such as an authenticator app.

4. Conditional Access
--> Controls access based on user, location, device compliance, application and risk conditions.
 
5. Roles and Administrators
--> Assign administrative permissions using roles such as Global Administrator, User Administrator and Application Administrator.
